1
00:00:01,641 --> 00:00:04,480
The Hungry Metal Cardbot

2
00:00:15,957 --> 00:00:18,309
Was there an accident?

3
00:00:19,858 --> 00:00:20,984
Excuse me?

4
00:00:21,687 --> 00:00:22,934
Are you alright?

5
00:00:24,768 --> 00:00:26,660
H-Hello?

6
00:00:28,184 --> 00:00:30,140
Hungry...

7
00:00:30,995 --> 00:00:32,390
Aah!

8
00:00:53,301 --> 00:00:57,612
We received a report that a monster truck transformed into a robot

9
00:00:57,612 --> 00:01:01,323
and ate a battery from an electric car that was passing by on Route 66 last night.

10
00:01:01,323 --> 00:01:05,186
I'm telling you! A gaudy looking truck suddenly started saying it was hungry, and it transformed into a robot...

11
00:01:05,186 --> 00:01:06,849
Mmph? Could this be?

12
00:01:06,849 --> 00:01:09,206
Yes. I'm sure it's a Metal Cardbot.

13
00:01:09,206 --> 00:01:09,950
Jun!

14
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,224
Stop watching TV or you'll be late for school again!

15
00:01:13,224 --> 00:01:13,980
Uh, right!

16
00:01:14,965 --> 00:01:16,120
I'll be off, then!

17
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:17,974
Do you know where it happened, Jun?

18
00:01:17,974 --> 00:01:19,664
Yes! By the countryside just outside Mowtown-

19
00:01:19,664 --> 00:01:20,715
What was that?

20
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,385
Hahaha, what's got you all jumpy, huh?

21
00:01:24,385 --> 00:01:27,140
Uh... Dad, what are you doing under the car?

22
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:28,944
Well, the car is acting a little strange.

23
00:01:28,944 --> 00:01:31,512
I think it's broken somewhere. But I just can't figure it out...

24
00:01:31,512 --> 00:01:33,758
Well, I'll be off to school then!

25
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:39,152
It hasn't been very long, but I had a great time here thanks to all of you.

26
00:01:39,152 --> 00:01:40,442
Thank you, everyone.

27
00:01:40,896 --> 00:01:43,098
Crest!!

28
00:01:43,098 --> 00:01:45,408
I'll never forget the fun times we had!

29
00:01:45,408 --> 00:01:47,307
We're friends for life-

30
00:01:47,307 --> 00:01:48,753
Oh no, Crest!

31
00:01:48,753 --> 00:01:51,200
I can't believe you're leaving us, Crest!

32
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:53,478
Oh, you mustn't forget me no matter what!

33
00:01:53,478 --> 00:01:55,462
Haha, thank you...

34
00:01:55,462 --> 00:01:58,420
He's been a big star from beginning to end.

35
00:01:58,420 --> 00:01:59,275
You said it!

36
00:01:59,275 --> 00:02:02,209
I hope things will be alright until the farewell party tonight.

37
00:02:02,209 --> 00:02:04,679
The news this morning didn't sound so good.

38
00:02:04,679 --> 00:02:09,949
Everyone's out there looking for the culprit now, so we'll find out soon enough- huh?

39
00:02:09,949 --> 00:02:11,485
Did you find something?

40
00:02:11,485 --> 00:02:14,675
I found traces of oil spilled by a Metal Cardbot.

41
00:02:14,675 --> 00:02:16,179
It might be from the culprit.

42
00:02:16,179 --> 00:02:17,877
Does that mean the culprit was injured?

43
00:02:17,877 --> 00:02:19,413
I can't say for sure.

44
00:02:19,413 --> 00:02:21,173
But it looks like he went downtown.

45
00:02:22,170 --> 00:02:23,901
Okay, I'll leave it to you then.

46
00:02:23,901 --> 00:02:25,574
You can count on me.

47
00:02:28,699 --> 00:02:31,682
What awful timing for the car to break down on the day of the party...

48
00:02:31,682 --> 00:02:35,223
I asked for a rental car, so it should be alright.

49
00:02:35,223 --> 00:02:36,996
Well, I'll be off then!

50
00:02:36,996 --> 00:02:38,210
Take care, honey!

51
00:02:38,703 --> 00:02:41,305
Time to prepare for the party.

52
00:02:48,750 --> 00:02:53,932
Ugh... Don't get it... Just ate...

53
00:02:53,932 --> 00:02:56,655
But me still hungry...

54
00:03:08,622 --> 00:03:10,179
Ah! Oh...

55
00:03:13,361 --> 00:03:14,496
Wha? What the?!

56
00:03:15,304 --> 00:03:17,175
Uh... uh...

57
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:20,300
When did he bring over the rental car?

58
00:03:23,703 --> 00:03:26,221
Hello? Oh, Edo!

59
00:03:26,221 --> 00:03:29,384
About the car. It seems like the tank is rusty.

60
00:03:29,384 --> 00:03:32,359
It's probably going to take about a week to fix.

61
00:03:32,359 --> 00:03:36,418
What? I'll have to drive around in that gaudy looking truck for a whole week?!

62
00:03:36,418 --> 00:03:40,877
What gaudy looking truck? I haven't sent the rental car over yet.

63
00:03:40,877 --> 00:03:43,426
But what about the one sitting right outside my-?

64
00:03:45,256 --> 00:03:46,167
Huh?

65
00:03:48,456 --> 00:03:52,966
Uh, Edo, I'm sorry. Forget about what I just said. I must have made a mistake.

66
00:03:52,966 --> 00:03:58,310
So, you said the repair would take a week? I'll wait for the rental car then.

67
00:03:58,310 --> 00:03:57,310
Please send a normal car.

68
00:03:58,310 --> 00:04:01,806
-Please send a normal car...
-Me can't... Wait any more! Aagh!

69
00:04:01,806 --> 00:04:05,918
Oh, in an hour? Don't worry, I'll be here. Alright...

70
00:04:07,124 --> 00:04:10,759
No more... WAITING!!

71
00:04:10,907 --> 00:04:14,193
Hello? Hello? Are you still there?

72
00:04:14,193 --> 00:04:17,273
A gaudy looking truck suddenly started saying it was hungry!

73
00:04:17,273 --> 00:04:20,137
Then it transformed into a robot and attacked my car!

74
00:04:20,137 --> 00:04:21,653
Huh... wait a minute!

75
00:04:25,896 --> 00:04:29,372
I found the trail of oil! It's going towards the residential area!

76
00:04:29,372 --> 00:04:31,394
That's where Jun's house is.

77
00:04:31,394 --> 00:04:32,396
Let's hurry!

78
00:04:32,899 --> 00:04:34,115
H-Hey! Hang on!

79
00:04:34,115 --> 00:04:35,374
Wait for us!

80
00:04:40,745 --> 00:04:43,564
Hungry...

81
00:04:43,564 --> 00:04:46,915
Want to... eat that.

82
00:04:47,569 --> 00:04:50,593
You want to eat... the generator?

83
00:04:50,593 --> 00:04:51,805
Gimme!

84
00:04:52,269 --> 00:04:54,177
Then you need to ask nicely!

85
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:56,408
I said no!

86
00:04:57,165 --> 00:04:59,170
And your hands are all dirty!

87
00:04:59,170 --> 00:04:59,747
Hold still.

88
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:03,000
There you go.

89
00:05:04,346 --> 00:05:07,608
Now. You have to say "thank you" before eating.

90
00:05:07,608 --> 00:05:09,110
Say, "Thank you for the food".

91
00:05:09,110 --> 00:05:11,567
Thank... you for the food.

92
00:05:12,930 --> 00:05:12,189
Hmph.

93
00:05:16,518 --> 00:05:17,689
Tasty...

94
00:05:17,689 --> 00:05:19,639
Good boy! There you go.

95
00:05:20,454 --> 00:05:22,348
See you tonight, Anna.

96
00:05:22,348 --> 00:05:24,269
Yeah, see you later!

97
00:05:24,269 --> 00:05:25,668
Take care!

98
00:05:26,754 --> 00:05:27,735
Jun.

99
00:05:27,735 --> 00:05:29,100
Blue Cop! Did you find him?

100
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:31,451
We found that the trail of oil is headed towards your neighborhood.

101
00:05:31,451 --> 00:05:32,509
What?!

102
00:05:32,713 --> 00:05:36,528
Jun! Jun!

103
00:05:36,528 --> 00:05:38,757
Get in. We have a problem at your place!

104
00:05:38,757 --> 00:05:40,629
Wha?! No way!

105
00:05:42,899 --> 00:05:44,408
Huh... what's wrong?

106
00:05:44,408 --> 00:05:45,600
Still hungry.

107
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:46,682
Huh?

108
00:05:46,682 --> 00:05:49,369
Is there a problem with the voltage?

109
00:05:49,369 --> 00:05:50,141
Hm?

110
00:05:51,908 --> 00:05:54,293
Hold on. Excuse me.

111
00:05:56,846 --> 00:06:00,165
Oh dear. You have a nail in your backside!

112
00:06:00,165 --> 00:06:01,997
This must be the problem.

113
00:06:03,487 --> 00:06:05,264
Stick out your bottom for me.

114
00:06:05,264 --> 00:06:06,677
Like this?

115
00:06:06,677 --> 00:06:08,446
Just like that.

116
00:06:08,935 --> 00:06:11,526
Oh, you poor thing...

117
00:06:12,786 --> 00:06:14,112
Just hang in there.

118
00:06:35,716 --> 00:06:37,257
There, all better!

119
00:06:42,259 --> 00:06:44,608
T-Thank you!

120
00:06:44,608 --> 00:06:46,161
Don't mention it.

121
00:06:46,161 --> 00:06:48,233
But, who are you, anyway?

122
00:06:48,233 --> 00:06:50,581
Me... Buffalo Crush.

123
00:06:50,581 --> 00:06:53,100
I'm Yuri. Finish your meal.

124
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:53,942
Ok.

125
00:06:59,432 --> 00:07:01,774
He's in our yard?!

126
00:07:03,305 --> 00:07:05,836
Hey, hot pink! What are you doing in my yard?!

127
00:07:05,836 --> 00:07:06,918
Mom?!

128
00:07:08,915 --> 00:07:11,990
Leave my mom alone, right now!

129
00:07:13,365 --> 00:07:14,278
Huh?

130
00:07:14,278 --> 00:07:17,276
Deus Machina's treasure! Metal Breath!

131
00:07:18,596 --> 00:07:21,858
That! Give it here!

132
00:07:22,132 --> 00:07:24,968
So this is why you're taking my mom hostage, huh?!

133
00:07:24,968 --> 00:07:27,257
Hostage? What you mean?

134
00:07:30,471 --> 00:07:31,894
That's enough.

135
00:07:32,290 --> 00:07:35,240
If you're done eating, you should say "thank you for the food!"

136
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:37,374
Huh?! Thank you for the food.

137
00:07:37,889 --> 00:07:38,927
Jun.

138
00:07:38,927 --> 00:07:41,437
Wild Guardy and I will be at your house soon.

139
00:07:41,437 --> 00:07:43,877
I'm at my house right now. Please hurry.

140
00:07:43,877 --> 00:07:45,230
What? Okay.

141
00:07:46,177 --> 00:07:48,689
Uh... I have something to discuss with you about the repairs.

142
00:07:48,689 --> 00:07:51,572
What? But I have to prepare for the party...

143
00:07:57,579 --> 00:07:58,687
That's Edo's car!

144
00:08:01,588 --> 00:08:03,117
Jun! Are you alright?

145
00:08:03,117 --> 00:08:04,661
Blue Cop! Wild Guardy!

146
00:08:04,661 --> 00:08:08,187
Is that Buffalo Crush? What is he doing here?

147
00:08:10,425 --> 00:08:11,584
Gimme that Metal Breath!

148
00:08:11,584 --> 00:08:12,605
Huh?!

149
00:08:12,946 --> 00:08:13,920
Blue Cop, setup!

150
00:08:18,942 --> 00:08:19,946
Wild Guardy!

151
00:08:32,966 --> 00:08:34,783
He's too strong!

152
00:08:34,783 --> 00:08:38,206
Buffalo Crush full!

153
00:08:38,206 --> 00:08:41,620
Now me unstoppable!

154
00:08:42,168 --> 00:08:43,869
Mega Trucker! Where are you?!

155
00:08:43,869 --> 00:08:44,913
Ugh.

156
00:08:44,913 --> 00:08:47,360
Come on, move it already!

157
00:08:50,922 --> 00:08:53,927
Don't let his strength get the better of you.

158
00:08:53,927 --> 00:08:55,985
Let's overwhelm him with a series of attacks!

159
00:08:55,985 --> 00:08:57,168
Understood!

160
00:09:00,105 --> 00:09:01,519
Wild Guardy, setup!

161
00:09:05,514 --> 00:09:07,201
Come on, then!

162
00:09:07,498 --> 00:09:09,134
That shield puny.

163
00:09:09,216 --> 00:09:10,778
Tomahawk Crush!

164
00:09:12,402 --> 00:09:13,311
Now we got you!

165
00:09:16,576 --> 00:09:19,240
Now! Megabolt Punch!

166
00:09:20,355 --> 00:09:21,360
Megabolt...

167
00:09:23,538 --> 00:09:25,480
Buffalo...

168
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:27,879
Moonsault!

169
00:09:35,743 --> 00:09:38,354
He's as impenetrable as my shield.

170
00:09:38,354 --> 00:09:40,975
Blue Cop! Let's finish this with Infinity Force Break!

171
00:09:40,975 --> 00:09:41,904
Got it!

172
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:44,269
Infinity...

173
00:09:46,370 --> 00:09:47,000
Force...

174
00:09:49,533 --> 00:09:51,268
Who's there?!

175
00:09:51,268 --> 00:09:55,239
Is this where you've been roaming about, Buffalo Crush?

176
00:09:55,239 --> 00:09:56,519
That sounds like...

177
00:09:56,519 --> 00:09:57,830
Buster Gallon?

178
00:09:57,830 --> 00:09:58,836
Who is that?!

179
00:09:58,836 --> 00:10:00,360
One of Black Hook's henchmen.

180
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:06,120
I'm back for the Metal Breath just like I promised, Earthling child.

181
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:08,325
I never invited you over to my house!

182
00:10:08,325 --> 00:10:10,365
And you're never getting the Metal Breath!

183
00:10:10,365 --> 00:10:15,274
If you want to turn this place into a battlefield, I have no objections!

184
00:10:20,567 --> 00:10:22,683
We leave now.

185
00:10:22,683 --> 00:10:24,288
Excuse me, you want us to what?

186
00:10:24,288 --> 00:10:27,557
Black Hook. You said before.

187
00:10:27,557 --> 00:10:31,142
Real Cardbot always pay back favor.

188
00:10:31,142 --> 00:10:33,100
Our restaurant's sticker?

189
00:10:34,921 --> 00:10:39,437
I suppose if you have your reasons...

190
00:10:39,437 --> 00:10:42,879
A foolish choice. The odds were in our favor.

191
00:10:42,879 --> 00:10:45,408
Set sails to the west. Let's go!

192
00:10:48,182 --> 00:10:50,712
What in the world just happened?

193
00:10:52,354 --> 00:10:55,798
I followed the trail of oil and found an escape pod in the mountains.

194
00:10:55,798 --> 00:10:58,489
Perhaps he was injured during the landing?

195
00:10:58,489 --> 00:11:01,250
And then Jun's mom fixed the oil leak.

196
00:11:01,250 --> 00:11:03,230
So that's what happened.

197
00:11:03,230 --> 00:11:05,211
She must have been surprised!

198
00:11:05,211 --> 00:11:08,990
So it's all thanks to your mother that we were able to have this party.

199
00:11:08,990 --> 00:11:10,219
It's nice but...

200
00:11:10,219 --> 00:11:13,326
Now that there are all these new enemies, I can't help but worry.

201
00:11:13,326 --> 00:11:15,657
I trust that you'll be able to handle them.

202
00:11:15,657 --> 00:11:16,788
I think so too!

203
00:11:16,788 --> 00:11:19,889
We'll be fine as long as we work together!

204
00:11:19,889 --> 00:11:21,774
Promise you'll visit us again, Crest!

205
00:11:21,774 --> 00:11:23,715
Mhm. Of course!

